e, "ipaRaw": "oʊkˈeɪ", "issues": ["SHORT_SENTENCE"], "grammar": [], "ipaAccent": "US", "exclusions": {}, "ipaVersion": "espeak-ng:1.52.0", "vocabulary": [], "clozeManual": false, "coarseEndMs": 345480, "contentKeys": {"IPA": "637302de296e54174edb9c4b299d7206558783de88b8ea10f7c7f7887f2bef63", "GRAMMAR": "20bcd758d04457aaba0d28bebd5010d230acf30aefb69757b1a828603c7e03f8", "LEXICAL": "e8f05963f52a30a94eb94ae376d686d7f621691bf17d28f98f61aef1a2212a55", "PROFILE": "74579c7cded53d95c0eb25f2a4585e81075fb73f09e2299431d675ae949a1ffe", "DICTATION": "08707a66a3642ff32fc2d4f2847b88e7b3c870dfc76c1fd1d674967662fbc669", "SHADOWING": "8ae3b9f38e9b1206ea24670c91a06f12cd98a492be9014411cce61218dca94a9", "TRANSLATION": "5b3f62aceba3c165a0e455ee96fa57e9038e3781589a36354fa79d0ad87209dd"}, "sourceWords": [], "translation": "Được rồi.", "contentStale": false, "manualFields": [], "timingSource": null, "coarseStartMs": 345000, "manualLocales": {}, "manualSources": {}, "thoughtGroups": [], "cefrSuggestion": "B1", "ipaNeedsReview": false, "contentWarnings": [], "dictationEligible": true, "dictationPriority": null, "dictationSelected": true, "ipaDisplayVersion": "learner-ipa-v1", "shadowingEligible": true, "shadowingPriority": null, "shadowingSelected": true, "contentTypeSuggestion": "MONOLOGUE"}]'::jsonb,NULL,'2026-11-19T18:41:42.084887+00:00','{"text": "Okay, let''s talk about why you should learn English while exercising. So, first of all, you should be active. You should do exercise, walk or ride a bike, hike, maybe exercise at the gym. You should be active. You should exercise and do things. It''s healthy for you, of course. We need this. We need to exercise. We need to work our muscles, our heart. All of that, and we should do this often. We should do this frequently, so more than once a week, hopefully. So, this is the first reason why you should do these two things together. Number one, it''s good for your health. And number two, it helps you find time to learn English. Okay. If you feel like you don''t have a lot of time in your day to exercise, to learn English, to spend time with your family, then you can combine two of these things. You can combine exercise and learning English, so that you have more time to do these things. So, if you''re watching this video right now, you''re practicing English, but you might not be doing anything else. Maybe you''re just sitting on the couch, or lying on your bed, or sitting at a table. But you can also listen to this video while you walk, for example. Or maybe you can go to the gym, and use the bicycle, and you can watch this video while you ride the bike, or while you walk on the treadmill. That machine at the gym, where you walk, you can combine this practice with some exercise. That''s a good idea. And when you do this, it can help you with your exercise because your brain is not only thinking about the exercise. For example, sometimes when you run, you''re just thinking about how hard it is, how tired you are, and so that makes it harder to run. But if you''re concentrated on an English podcast or an English video or something like that, your brain is not only thinking about the exercise and how hard it is. So that can help you with your. Exercise, and I think that when you do two things at the same time, like exercise and language learning, and those things are productive, they''re good. You feel very good about it. You feel productive. You feel satisfied because you''re doing two things that are good for you at the same time. I feel great when I practice my languages and exercise at the same time. It feels fantastic because I''m saving time. I''m spending time doing productive things. I''m being healthy, and it just feels good to do this. In general, I can''t multitask well. I''m very bad at multitasking, but I can walk and listen to something in another language, or even practice my speaking. I can do this. So if you feel like you can''t multitask well, you can probably still combine exercise and language learning, or some types of exercise maybe. So if I can do it, you can do it. And like I said, it feels great. You will feel good about yourself when you do this. Okay.", "language": "English", "segments": [{"text": "Okay, let''s talk about why you should learn English while exercising. So, first of all, you should be active. You should do exercise, walk or ride a bike, hike, maybe exercise at the gym. You should be active. You should exercise and do things. It''s healthy for you, of course. We need this. We need to exercise. We need to work our muscles, our heart. All of that, and we should do this often. We should do this frequently, so more than once a week, hopefully. So, this is the first reason why you should do these two things together. Number one, it''s good for your health. And number two, it helps you find time to learn English. Okay. If you feel like you don''t have a lot of time in your day to exercise, to learn English, to spend time with your family, then you can combine two of these things. You can combine exercise and learning English, so that you have more time to do these things.", "end_ms": 115000, "start_ms": 0}, {"text": "So, if you''re watching this video right now, you''re practicing English, but you might not be doing anything else. Maybe you''re just sitting on the couch, or lying on your bed, or sitting at a table. But you can also listen to this video while you walk, for example. Or maybe you can go to the gym, and use the bicycle, and you can watch this video while you ride the bike, or while you walk on the treadmill. That machine at the gym, where you walk, you can combine this practice with some exercise. That''s a good idea. And when you do this, it can help you with your exercise because your brain is not only thinking about the exercise. For example, sometimes when you run, you''re just thinking about how hard it is, how tired you are, and so that makes it harder to run. But if you''re concentrated on an English podcast or an English video or something like that, your brain is not only thinking about the exercise and how hard it is. So that can help you with your.", "end_ms": 230000, "start_ms": 115000}, {"text": "Exercise, and I think that when you do two things at the same time, like exercise and language learning, and those things are productive, they''re good. You feel very good about it. You feel productive. You feel satisfied because you''re doing two things that are good for you at the same time. I feel great when I practice my languages and exercise at the same time. It feels fantastic because I''m saving time. I''m spending time doing productive things. I''m being healthy, and it just feels good to do this. In general, I can''t multitask well. I''m very bad at multitasking, but I can walk and listen to something in another language, or even practice my speaking. I can do this. So if you feel like you can''t multitask well, you can probably still combine exercise and language learning, or some types of exercise maybe. So if I can do it, you can do it. And like I said, it feels great. You will feel good about yourself when you do this.", "end_ms": 345000, "start_ms": 230000}, {"text": "Okay.", "end_ms": 345979, "start_ms": 345000}], "timestamps": []}'::jsonb,'{"accent": "US", "locale": "vi-VN", "density": "AUTO", "activities": ["DICTATION", "SHADOWING"], "annotations": ["TRANSLATION", "LEXICAL", "GRAMMAR", "PROFILE"], "grammarLimit": 8, "vocabularyLimit": 20, "pronunciationProvider": "LOCAL", "pronunciationStrategy": "PREGENERATE"}'::jsonb,NULL,NULL,'{"key": "d3eeb01732bf9dd7c4356b52c8d32d0a40f1ebc28aa280f58c1557d4ff77245c", "cefr": "B1", "manual": false, "contentType": "MONOLOGUE"}'::jsonb,FALSE,NULL) ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
